# SAFE DEFAULT: do not pass the live SCRIMP working tree to Docker.
#
# This repository can contain hundreds of gigabytes of untracked
# simulation results. Directory negation patterns (!sandbox/, etc.)
# were NOT sufficient: BuildKit transferred >45 GB despite a
# Python-side 1.78 MiB audit.
#
# Direct "docker build ... ." is therefore deliberately unsupported.
# Use scripts/build-v130-docker-candidate.sh, which stages ONLY audited
# Git-tracked source files in a temporary external context and builds
# from that physically isolated directory. The staged context has its
# own small .dockerignore, not this deny-all guard.
**
